    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Secondary dominants temporarily treat a non-tonic chord as a local key centre."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "labelling",
      "title": "Labelling",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A7 in C major = V7/vi (resolves to Dm). D7 = V7/V (resolves to G). Accidentals foreign to home key signature signal their presence."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "in-repertoire",
      "title": "In repertoire",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "O'Carolan arrangements, ragtime hornpipes, contemporary folk songwriting. V7/vi→vi brightens briefly before returning to I."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "detection",
      "title": "Detection",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Sudden sharpened note outside key for one bar? Suspect secondary dominant or modal mixture."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
